            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@justinmk \r\nYes, I ran into this while working on a markdown plugin (not published yet). Its `foldexpr` parses the buffer with treesitter. It runs after the put has added its lines but before the leftover line is deleted, and that deletion is never reported through on_bytes, so the tree keeps a line that no longer exists. Other plugins (e.g. render-markdown) then fail with \"Index out of bounds\". For now I work around it by rebuilding the tree on `TextChanged` when its end doesn't match the buffer size.\r\n\r\nMinimal repro (`nvim --clean -l repro.lua`):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, true, { 'x', 'y' })\r\nlocal parser = vim.treesitter.get_parser(0, 'markdown')\r\nfunction _G.foldexpr()\r\n  parser:parse()\r\n  return 0\r\nend\r\nvim.wo.foldmethod = 'expr'\r\nvim.wo.foldexpr = 'v:lua.foldexpr()'\r\n\r\nvim.fn.setreg('a', { '# foo', 'bar' }, 'l')\r\nvim.cmd('normal! ggVG\"ap')\r\n\r\nlocal root = parser:parse()[1]:root()\r\nprint(vim.inspect({ root:range() }), vim.api.nvim_buf_line_count(0))\r\nprint(vim.treesitter.get_node_text(root, 0))\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn 0.12.5:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{ 0, 0, 3, 0 } 2\r\nE5113: Lua chunk: .../runtime/lua/vim/treesitter.lua:216: Index out of bounds\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this PR the root range is `{ 0, 0, 2, 0 }` and the text is returned.\r\n\r\nThanks for the findings. I've reworked the PR:\r\n\r\n- The leftover line is now deleted with `del_lines()`, which covers undo, the cursor fix-up before callbacks, and adjusting marks and extmarks. This addresses 3, 5 and 6; the manual `extmark_adjust()` / `deleted_lines()` calls are gone.\r\n- The deletion is skipped when the buffer is still `ML_EMPTY` (the put failed), which fixes 1 and 2. I confirmed 2, including that `'modified'` gets set even with `'nomodifiable'`.\r\n- 4: left as is. `del_lines()` also ignores the return value of `ml_delete_flags()`, so this path now behaves like other line deletions.\r\n- 7: I extended the \"visual paste\" group in `lua/buffer_updates_spec.lua` with new numbered cases (each needs a different starting buffer): redo, `gp` (callbacks never see the cursor past the last line), a failed put followed by `u`, and failed puts in an empty buffer (including `'nomodifiable'`) that check `'modified'` and changedtick. `editor/put_spec.lua` checks that the cursor in another window is adjusted (before the fix it was left on line 3 of a 2-line buffer). All of these fail without the fix.\r\n",
